      "evidence_state": "PARTIAL",
      "source_fields": [
        "/arm_contrast/trials"
      ],
      "rendered_text": "<div class='absent'><strong>Randomised-contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the registry arm structure &mdash; disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. For each pooled trial the randomised contrast is reconstructed from AACT <code>design_groups</code> + <code>interventions</code>: <strong>0 of 3</strong> pooled trials have a registry-confirmed contrast (the intervention of interest differs across arms). A trial with no registry arm data, or coded under a class label / development code we cannot machine-match, is shown as <em>contrast unverified</em> &mdash; a VISIBLE fail-open state, never silently treated as verified. <table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Contrast status</th><th>Randomised difference</th></tr><tr><td>11172832</td><td>unverified_no_registry_match</td><td title='no NCT/registry match for this pooled trial; the randomised contrast of the intervention of interest cannot be registry-confirmed.'>&amp;mdash;</td></tr><tr><td>16769748</td><td>unverified_no_registry_match</td><td title='no NCT/registry match for this pooled trial; the randomised contrast of the intervention of interest cannot be registry-confirmed.'>&amp;mdash;</td></tr><tr><td>19522426</td><td>unverified_no_registry_match</td><td title='no NCT/registry match for this pooled trial; the randomised contrast of the intervention of interest cannot be registry-confirmed.'>&amp;mdash;</td></tr></table></div>",
